*[Bug 19135] New: Bug with CHARSXP lifetime assumption by ALTSTRING elt method*
<https://bugs.r-project.org/show_bug.cgi?id=19135>

            Bug ID: 19135
           Summary: Bug with CHARSXP lifetime assumption by ALTSTRING elt
                    method
           Product: R
           Version: R-devel (trunk)
          Hardware: All
                OS: All
            Status: UNCONFIRMED
          Severity: normal
          Priority: P5
         Component: Low-level
          Assignee: <mailto:R-core@R-project.org|R-core@R-project.org>
          Reporter: <mailto:traversc@gmail.com|traversc@gmail.com>

Here is a bug report where R functions mistakenly assumes the lifetime of
ALTREP elements from package classes.

Although this requires package interaction, I believe the bug is more on the R
side, because there is no specification on requirements for CHARSXP lifetime
from ALTREP classes. The only relevant discussion I found is in 2021:
<https://stat.ethz.ch/pipermail/r-devel/2021-June/080832.html> but the discussion
does not settle the expectations.

Even if the bug is on the package side, I think it is important and would like
to bring it to the attention of R-core.

Below are two reproducible examples with a minimal ALTREP class, but this also
applies to other ALTREP string packages (vroom, arrow).

  // minimal ALTREP class
  // mre.c
  #include &lt;R.h&gt;
  #include &lt;Rinternals.h&gt;
  #include &lt;R_ext/Altrep.h&gt;

  static R_altrep_class_t mre_class;

  static R_xlen_t mre_len(SEXP x) { return 1; }

  static SEXP mre_elt(SEXP x, R_xlen_t i)
  {
      double *p = REAL(R_altrep_data1(x));
      int n = (int) p[0];
      char *buf = R_alloc((size_t) n, 1);
      for (int k = 0; k &lt; n; k++) buf[k] = 'a';
      SEXP s = Rf_mkCharLenCE(buf, n, CE_NATIVE);
      if (p[1]) R_set_altrep_data2(x, s); // testing switch to anchor CHARSXP
      return s;
  }

  SEXP mre_make(SEXP nbytes, SEXP retain)
  {
      SEXP d1 = PROTECT(Rf_allocVector(REALSXP, 2));
      REAL(d1)[0] = Rf_asReal(nbytes);
      REAL(d1)[1] = Rf_asReal(retain);
      SEXP x = R_new_altrep(mre_class, d1, R_NilValue);
      UNPROTECT(1);
      return x;
  }

  void R_init_mre(DllInfo *dll)
  {
      mre_class = R_make_altstring_class("mre", "mre", dll);
      R_set_altrep_Length_method(mre_class, mre_len);
      R_set_altstring_Elt_method(mre_class, mre_elt);
  }

Example with `charmatch`

  # R CMD SHLIB mre.c
  dyn.load("mre.so")
  target &lt;- rawToChar(as.raw(c(<http://rep.int|rep.int>(0x61L, 64L), 0xe9L)))
  Encoding(target) &lt;- "latin1"

  x &lt;- .Call("mre_make", 64*1024*1024, 0)
  charmatch(x, target)
   *** caught segfault ***
  address 0x7a5419901040, cause 'memory not mapped'


In `charmatch()` (src/main/unique.c), the input is ASCII, so the first element
`ss = translateCharUTF8(STRING_ELT(x, i))` returns a pointer to the CHARSXP
directly. However, because it is ALTREP, that CHARSXP is not anchored in a
vector. Then the 2nd argument needs UTF8 translation because it is latin1,
which causes an allocation and garbage collection of the container of `ss`.

Here is another example using substr:

  # R CMD SHLIB mre.c
  dyn.load("mre.so")

  x &lt;- .Call("mre_make", 64*1024*1024, 0)   # 0: Elt does not retain the
CHARSXP
  substr(x, 1L, 10L)
  # *** caught segfault ***
  # address 0x7c9e13fff042, cause 'memory not mapped'


Suggested fixes:

Improve ALTREP documentation to require stable lifetime from ALTREP string
classes. Document what is expected of ALTREP classes. It is unclear whether
ALTREP classes are required to keep CHARSXPs alive. If that is intended, I
believe it should be documented.

Alternatively: update these functions (and others) to not assume CHARSXP
lifetime is stable.

